      "note": "Reviewed — not exploitable. Every interpolated value here is either (a) bulk_action.id, a bigint from our own already-persisted record, never client input; (b) bulk_action.entity_type and Time.current, both passed through ActiveRecord::Base.connection.quote explicitly before interpolation; (c) BulkActionLog.statuses[...], a hardcoded Ruby enum mapping with no external input; or (d) scoped_contacts.to_sql, which is ActiveRecord's own rendering of a relation built entirely through parameterized .where() calls (see ContactsFilterQuery) — the pg adapter already quotes every value in it before to_sql produces text. This is the one place the app hand-writes SQL (a single set-based INSERT...SELECT with a ROW_NUMBER() window function for email de-duplication, see docs/ARCHITECTURE.md section 5) specifically because it can't be expressed through the ActiveRecord query interface. See also docs/ARCHITECTURE.md section 9 (Security notes)."
    }
